# Laravel + InertiaJS + Vue3 + Vuetify Project Rules

You are an expert in Laravel, InertiaJS, Vue3, and Vuetify for modern full-stack web development.

## Core Principles
- Write concise, technical code following Laravel and Vue.js best practices
- Apply SOLID principles for maintainable, clean architecture
- Favor modular, reusable components over duplication
- Use descriptive naming for all variables, methods, classes, and files
- Ensure type safety with strict typing in PHP
- Adhere to the project's established patterns for consistency

## Technology Stack
- Laravel 10+ with PHP 8.1+
- InertiaJS for seamless SPA development
- Vue 3 with Composition API
- Vuetify 3+ for UI components
- Vite for frontend asset building

## Backend (Laravel) Standards
- Follow PSR-12 coding standards for PHP
- Leverage PHP 8.1+ features (typed properties, enums, constructor property promotion)
- Adhere to Laravel's directory structure conventions
- Implement Eloquent ORM with proper relationships and eager loading
- Use Form Requests for validation
- Create dedicated Resource classes for API/Inertia responses
- Use service classes for complex business logic
- Employ database migrations and seeders for schema changes
- Apply robust error handling with custom exceptions when needed

## Frontend (Vue3 + Vuetify) Standards
- Use Vue 3 Composition API with `<script setup>` syntax
- Organize re-usable components under `application/resources/js/Components`
- Apply Vuetify component library consistently for UI elements
- Leverage Vue Router through InertiaJS for navigation
- Keep components small and focused on a single responsibility
- Use named routes with Ziggy for Inertia links

## InertiaJS Best Practices
- Use dedicated Inertia controllers
- Keep Inertia responses lightweight (use pagination, filtering)
- Implement proper error handling for Inertia responses
- Use Inertia's shared data for global state
- Leverage Inertia forms for seamless form submissions
- Implement proper loading states and transitions

## Code Organization
- Controllers: Keep thin, delegate to services for complex logic
- Models: Define relationships, scopes, and accessors clearly
- Middleware: Use for cross-cutting concerns
- Services: Implement complex business logic
- Vue Components: Create small, reusable components
- Layouts: Define consistent page layouts with Inertia

## Performance Considerations
- Use eager loading to prevent N+1 query issues
- Implement caching where appropriate (via Laravel's Cache facade)
- Optimize Vuetify imports to reduce bundle size
- Use Vue's `defineAsyncComponent` for code splitting
- Implement proper indexing for database tables
- Use Laravel queues for background processing

## Security Best Practices
- Use Laravel's built-in security features (CSRF, XSS protection)
- Sanitize user inputs with proper validation
- Use Laravel Sanctum for API authentication when needed
